{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\nNothing validates, before a reconcile pass mutates a live client Jira, that the mapped\nprojects EXIST / are visible to the bridge bot. Two live-only failure modes:\n1. A mapped-but-nonexistent (decommissioned / permission-lost) project key is syntactically\n   valid, so `_validate_project_key` passes; the failure only surfaces deep in fan-out as an\n   ACLI error. This is exactly the `05b8-4efe-8d58-4c27` incident class.\n2. `resolve_project` (projects_store.py) returns `mapping.legacy_default` VERBATIM,\n   unvalidated. Every unbound/legacy ticket (absent bridge_project) resolves there. The\n   cross-project write guard's allowed set = `read_projects().keys()` and EXCLUDES creates\n   (applier.py `_cross_project_targets`), so a legacy_default pointing at a real-but-wrong\n   (or nonexistent) project drives a mass CREATE storm into the wrong place, unguarded.\n\n## Approach\nAdd a reconcile-pass PREFLIGHT that runs BEFORE any outbound mutation and validates every\nproject the pass could touch is visible to the configured backend.\n\nRequired-key set (single source of truth, mirrors the fetcher fan-out at fetcher.py:540 so it\nvalidates exactly what fan-out queries): `read_projects(repo_root).keys()`; when that mapping\nis EMPTY the fetcher falls back to the single configured backend `query_project`\n(`[_query_project]`) — the exact green-state incident shape `{legacy_default:'REB',\nprojects:{}}` — so the preflight INCLUDES that fallback `query_project` when `projects` is\nempty. PLUS `legacy_default` (when non-empty), since `resolve_project` sends every\nunbound/legacy create there. Empty-and-no-fallback → nothing to check (never probes).\n\nProbe transport: reuse `access_check.py`'s existing `AcliClient` transport and its retry\nhelper (`_retry_sleep` / `JQL_RETRY_COUNT`). Enumerate bot-visible keys through the client's\nALREADY-PRESENT generic REST accessor `AcliClient._direct_rest_get` (acli_rest.py:207 — used\nby `get_issue_property`, `transition_issue`, `validate_assignee_exists`) against the standard\nJira Cloud \"Get projects paginated\" endpoint `GET /rest/api/3/project/search`, walking pages\nvia `startAt` and the envelope's `values[].key` / `isLast`. Pagination terminates on `isLast`,\nan empty `values` page, or a hard page cap (guard against a server that never sets `isLast`).\nNo new transport class or subprocess.\n\nRetry vs hard fail: a retryable transport error is retried up to `JQL_RETRY_COUNT` with the\n`_retry_sleep` backoff; if still unreachable it raises a distinct `TransportUnavailableError`\n(fail-closed, own message), separate from `ProjectVisibilityError` (a reachable backend that\ndoes not list a required key).\n\nReusable single source of truth: an importable `access_check.py` function\n`check_mapped_project_visibility(repo_root, *, client=..., query_project=..., ...)` returning a\nstructured `ProjectVisibilityResult` (`status` in {`ok`,`missing`,`transport_unavailable`,\n`skipped`}), plus an `enforce_*` wrapper that raises. Ticket `9702` (bridge fsck live\ndiagnostic) reuses this exact function — NOT inlined into the reconcile pass.\n\nBackend-neutrality: the WIRING GATES ON THE BACKEND — it reads\n`rebar.config.load_config().reconciler.backend` and only builds the Cloud `AcliClient` and\nprobes when that key is `\"jira\"`. Any other backend (e.g. `\"jira-datacenter\"`, whose\npycontribs transport has no `_direct_rest_get`) logs an observable \"skipped: backend <key> has\nno visible-projects probe\" and returns without a Cloud client. Defence in depth: the helper\nreturns `status=\"skipped\"` if handed a client lacking a callable `_direct_rest_get`.\n\nWiring + result classification: wired at `__main__.py` `run_pass_result`, STRICTLY BEFORE\n`reconcile.reconcile_once` (the only outbound-mutation call), only for mutating passes.\nRead-only passes are skipped by concrete pre-`reconcile_once` signals: `route == \"preview\"`,\nand `target_mode.value in {\"dry-run\",\"reconcile-check\"}` (`reconcile-check` is already\nshort-circuited in `main()`; `no_write` is computed INSIDE `reconcile_once`, after this point,\nso it is NOT used here). A preflight failure is CONVERTED INTO a classified `PassResult`\n(`_Disposition.OPERATIONAL_FAILURE`, exit 1) like the existing `reconcile_once` path — never\nan uncaught raise, so the `run_pass` / `_lib_ops.py` consumers do not crash. The\nmissing-project message names the offending key(s) + the fix; observable via stderr/log.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A pass with a mapped key not visible to the bot aborts at preflight naming the key\n      BEFORE any Jira write — `reconcile.reconcile_once` NOT called; `run_pass_result` returns\n      an `OPERATIONAL_FAILURE` `PassResult`. Verified by\n      `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_preflight_project_visibility.py -q`.\n- [ ] `legacy_default` (when non-empty) is in the check; an invisible `legacy_default` is\n      caught, naming it. Verified by the same test module.\n- [ ] When `projects` is empty, the configured `query_project` fallback is included, so an\n      invisible fallback is caught. Verified by the same test module.\n- [ ] An all-visible mapping passes and the pass proceeds unchanged (`reconcile.reconcile_once`\n      is called; no happy-path change). Verified by the same test module.\n- [ ] A hard auth/transport error fails closed with a distinct transport-unavailable message\n      and is observable via log/stderr. Verified by the same test module.\n- [ ] A non-Cloud backend (`config.reconciler.backend != \"jira\"`) and a client lacking\n      `_direct_rest_get` are both skipped (observable) and the pass proceeds without a Cloud\n      client. Verified by the same test module.\n\n## Testing\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_preflight_project_visibility.py -q` —\n  fake/injected transport (no live Jira). Helper: fake client `_direct_rest_get` returns\n  `project/search` pages listing `{GOOD}` / `BAD` absent → `enforce_*` raises\n  `ProjectVisibilityError` naming `BAD`; all-visible → `status=\"ok\"`; `legacy_default=WRONG`\n  caught; empty `projects` + `query_project=FALL` (not visible) caught; `_direct_rest_get`\n  raising → `TransportUnavailableError`; no `_direct_rest_get` → `status=\"skipped\"`; multi-page\n  `values` all collected. Wiring (`run_pass_result` with stubbed `reconcile_once`): missing →\n  NOT called + `OPERATIONAL_FAILURE`; transport-unavailable → NOT called + `OPERATIONAL_FAILURE`;\n  all-visible → called once; `route==\"preview\"`, `target_mode.value==\"dry-run\"`, and a\n  non-`\"jira\"` backend each skip the probe and proceed. RED first: without the preflight the\n  pass proceeds to fan-out on an invisible key.\n- No unit test hits live Jira; the real envelope/pagination is unit-tested against the\n  documented Jira Cloud shape, live verification deferred to the existing\n  `rebar bridge access-check` / staging path (same transport/credentials).\n- `make lint` and `make typecheck` from the worktree.\n\n## Sequencing\nLives in `access_check.py` (new importable reusable helper) + wiring at `__main__.py`\n`run_pass_result`. Disjoint from A/B/C/E files. Reads projects_store (no edit)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786814867987862001,"uuid":"f378215c-5f7f-4945-90f1-e1a35889f901"}